---
import ProjectModal from "../components/ProjectModal.astro";
---

<ProjectModal
  id="account-project"
  ariaLabel="Accountancy project"
>
  <article class="account-project">
    <section class="project-hero">
      <div class="project-hero-top">
        <span>02 / SELECTED WORK</span>
        <span>2025 → 2026</span>
      </div>

      <h1>Accountancy</h1>

      <p class="project-tagline">
        Finding the transactions
        worth a closer look.
      </p>

      <p class="project-supporting">
        As part of my work, I had the opportunity to work on a financial
        data review and reconciliation system in response to a client's
        request: help their team make sense of customer files and find
        the transactions that need attention.
      </p>

      <div class="project-meta">
        <span>CLIENT PRESENTATION</span>
        <span>LLM API Gateway</span>
        <span>SCIKIT-LEARN</span>
        <span>LLM CLASSIFICATION</span>
        <span>NUMPY</span>
        <span>OLLAMA</span>
        <span>PYTHON</span>
      </div>

    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <div class="demo-video-frame">
        <video
          class="demo-video"
          data-project-autoplay
          loop
          muted
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          aria-label="Accountancy project demo"
        >
          <source src="/videos/accountancy/accountancy.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser does not support embedded video.
        </video>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="intro-grid">
      <div class="intro-block">
        <span class="section-number">01</span>
        <h2>What the client said.</h2>
        <p>
          The client said their customers often send all their files at once,
          leaving the team with a mix of transaction exports, bank statements
          and other records. It can be hard to know which files to look at
          first, what to look for, or whether there are any outliers in the
          data. They wanted help organising those files and identifying
          the items worth a closer look.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="intro-block">
        <span class="section-number">02</span>
        <h2>What I worked on.</h2>
        <p>
          My work focused on a reusable financial data pipeline that prepares files,
          identifies important columns, converts them into canonical schemas,
          runs deterministic review checks and presents the resulting signals
          in a Streamlit workspace. The system helps an accountant decide what
          deserves attention without pretending that a signal is proof of an error.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>UNDER THE HOOD</span>
        <h2>From raw export<br />to useful review.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-flow">
        <div class="architecture-node"><span>01</span><strong>Raw files</strong><small>Transaction exports and bank statements from different sources</small></div>
        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>
        <div class="architecture-node"><span>02</span><strong>Preparation</strong><small>CSV reading, inspection and source-column profiling</small></div>
        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>
        <div class="architecture-node"><span>03</span><strong>Identification</strong><small>Dates, amounts, descriptions and balances mapped by evidence</small></div>
        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>
        <div class="architecture-node"><span>04</span><strong>Normalisation</strong><small>Different source layouts converted into canonical datasets</small></div>
        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>
        <div class="architecture-node"><span>05</span><strong>Review logic</strong><small>Anomaly, recurring and behavioural checks with evidence</small></div>
        <div class="architecture-arrow">→</div>
        <div class="architecture-node"><span>06</span><strong>Accountant UI</strong><small>Prioritised signals, affected rows, charts and decisions</small></div>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-detail">
        <div>
          <span>DESIGN PRINCIPLE</span>
          <h3>A signal should explain itself.</h3>
          <p>
            Every review item is designed to answer three questions: what was
            unusual, why was it highlighted, and which rows should be checked?
            Findings use plain-English explanations and supporting evidence so
            the accountant stays in control of the final judgement.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span>REVIEW SIGNAL</span>
          <strong>“A supplier normally receives around £2,000. This payment is £10,000.”</strong>
          <small>Contextual comparison · affected rows · accountant decision</small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="features-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>SOME USEFUL THINGS</span>
        <h2>What Accountancy actually does.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card"><span>01</span><h3>Explainable anomaly review</h3><p>Highlights unusually large transactions, unusual daily activity, round numbers, repeated amounts, weak descriptions and other patterns that may deserve investigation.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span>02</span><h3>Behavioural context</h3><p>Compares activity within meaningful groups such as business categories or counterparties, so a payment is judged against the population where it actually belongs.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span>03</span><h3>Recurring payment analysis</h3><p>Learns repeated monthly or quarterly activity and surfaces missing payments, sharp amount changes and possible duplicate recurring transactions.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span>04</span><h3>Transaction reconciliation</h3><p>Compares transaction data with bank movements using exact, tolerant and split matching, while preserving ambiguous and unmatched cases for human review.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span>05</span><h3>Evidence-first interface</h3><p>The Items to review table gives every signal a priority, analysis type, plain-English explanation and affected-row count before opening the underlying evidence.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span>06</span><h3>Failure-aware pipeline</h3><p>Each file, review check and reconciliation service is isolated, allowing usable results to survive partial failures and making limitations visible instead of hiding them.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="decision-section">
      <span class="decision-number">03</span>
      <div>
        <span class="decision-label">THE ACCOUNTANT STAYS IN CONTROL</span>
        <h2>Different does not automatically mean wrong.</h2>
        <p>
          The interface is deliberately built around investigation rather than
          automatic conclusions. An accountant can open a signal, inspect its
          affected transactions, compare it with normal historical activity,
          review charts and supporting evidence, and mark it as expected when
          the explanation is satisfactory.
        </p>
        <p class="testing-note">
          The current synthetic demo includes clear examples of an unusually
          large payment, missing monthly and quarterly payments, a recurring
          supplier payment that increases sharply, and a possible duplicate payment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-ending">
      <p class="ending-label">Built as a foundation for a wider accounting SaaS platform and built Streamlit front end for a client presentation.</p>
      <h2>Messy records in.<br />Clearer reviews out.</h2>
      <p class="ending-supporting">
        Designed around reusable data contracts, explainable checks and an
        accountant-led review workflow.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</ProjectModal>

<style>
  .account-project { width: 100%; background: radial-gradient(circle at 8% 8%, #D2D9E1 0%, transparent 34%), radial-gradient(circle at 94% 18%, #93A7C1 0%, transparent 32%), radial-gradient(circle at 72% 74%, #B5C2D1 0%, transparent 38%), radial-gradient(circle at 18% 88%, #A8B7C9 0%, transparent 30%), linear-gradient(135deg, #D2D9E1 0%, #C6D0DB 48%, #D2D9E1 100%); color: #111; }
  .account-project strong { color: inherit; }
  .project-hero { position: relative; min-height: 88vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end; padding: 70px; }
  .project-hero-top { position: absolute; top: 28px; left: 70px; right: 90px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font: .74rem "Courier Prime", monospace; letter-spacing: .06em; color: #475569; }
  .project-hero h1 { margin: 0; font: 400 clamp(4rem, 11vw, 10rem)/.9 "Instrument Serif", serif; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .project-tagline { max-width: 800px; margin: 42px 0 20px; font: 400 clamp(2rem, 3.4vw, 3.6rem)/.98 "Instrument Serif", serif; }
  .project-supporting, .intro-block p, .architecture-detail p, .feature-card p, .decision-section p, .ending-supporting { max-width: 720px; font: 1rem/1.6 "Courier Prime", monospace; color: #3E4E63; }
  .project-supporting { margin: 0; }
  .project-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 9px; }
  .project-meta { margin-top: 28px; }
  .project-meta span { padding: 10px 14px; border: 1px solid #1113; border-radius: 999px; font: .72rem "Courier Prime", monospace; letter-spacing: .025em; }
  .demo-section { padding: 0 70px 110px; }
  .demo-video-frame { overflow: hidden; border-radius: 22px; background: #23354C; }
  .demo-video { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .section-heading > span, .architecture-detail span, .decision-label, .ending-label { font: .74rem "Courier Prime", monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .intro-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 70px; padding: 20px 70px 130px; }
  .intro-block { padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #1113; }
  .section-number { font: .74rem "Courier Prime", monospace; color: #475569; }
  .intro-block h2, .section-heading h2, .architecture-detail h3, .decision-section h2, .project-ending h2 { font-family: "Instrument Serif", serif; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .intro-block h2 { margin: 20px 0; font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 4vw, 4.6rem); line-height: .95; }
  .intro-block p { margin: 0; }
  .architecture-section { padding: 110px 70px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #23354C, #344B68 52%, #475F7D); color: #EAE6DF; }
  .architecture-section .section-heading > span, .architecture-detail span { color: #C6D0DB; }
  .section-heading { margin-bottom: 54px; }
  .section-heading h2 { max-width: 900px; margin: 14px 0 0; font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 6vw, 7rem); line-height: .9; }
  .architecture-flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr) auto) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .architecture-node { min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; min-height: 205px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; gap: 18px; padding: 23px; border: 1px solid #fff3; border-radius: 14px; }
  .architecture-node span, .architecture-node small { font-family: "Courier Prime", monospace; }
  .architecture-node span { font-size: .7rem; color: #A8B7C9; }
  .architecture-node strong { font: 400 1.82rem/1 "Instrument Serif", serif; color: #EAE6DF; }
  .architecture-node small { max-width: 170px; font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.45; color: #B5C2D1; }
  .architecture-arrow { color: #C6D0DB; }
  .architecture-detail { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr; gap: 60px; align-items: center; margin-top: 100px; padding-top: 80px; border-top: 1px solid #fff3; }
  .architecture-detail h3 { margin: 16px 0 24px; font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw, 4.5rem); line-height: .93; }
  .architecture-detail p { margin: 0; color: #D2D9E1; }
  .principle-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px; padding: 32px; border: 1px solid #fff3; border-radius: 18px; background: #ffffff0d; }
  .principle-card strong { font: 400 clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 4rem)/.98 "Instrument Serif", serif; }
  .principle-card small { color: #C6D0DB; font: .78rem/1.5 "Courier Prime", monospace; }
  .features-section { padding: 130px 70px; background: #EAE6DFaa; }
  .features-section .section-heading h2 { max-width: 950px; }
  .feature-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 18px; }
  .feature-card { min-height: 300px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 27px; border: 1px solid #1112; border-radius: 18px; background: #EAE6DFbb; }
  .feature-card:nth-child(even) { background: #C6D0DBaa; }
  .feature-card > span { font: .72rem "Courier Prime", monospace; color: #475569; }
  .feature-card h3 { margin: auto 0 20px; font: 400 clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3.7rem)/.95 "Instrument Serif", serif; }
  .feature-card p { margin: 0; font-size: .95rem; }
  .decision-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; gap: 40px; padding: 130px 70px; background: #B5C2D1; }
  .decision-number { font: .74rem "Courier Prime", monospace; color: #475569; }
  .decision-section h2 { max-width: 900px; margin: 18px 0 28px; font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 7.5rem); line-height: .88; }
  .decision-section p { margin: 0; color: #3E4E63; }
  .testing-note { max-width: 720px; margin-top: 28px !important; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #1112; font-size: .82rem !important; }
  .project-ending { min-height: 80vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; padding: 120px 70px; background: #EAE6DF99; }
  .project-ending h2 { max-width: 1000px; margin: 24px 0 28px; font-size: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 8rem); line-height: .84; }
  .ending-supporting { margin: 0 0 44px; }
  @media (min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1350px) { .architecture-flow { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 18px; } .architecture-arrow { display: none; } .architecture-node { min-height: 170px; } .architecture-node small { max-width: none; } }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .project-hero { min-height: 88dvh; padding: 90px 20px 40px; } .project-hero-top { top: 20px; left: 20px; right: 72px; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: .6rem; } .project-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 15vw, 6rem); } .project-tagline { margin: 30px 0 18px; font-size: clamp(2rem, 10vw, 2.8rem); } .project-supporting, .intro-block p, .feature-card p, .decision-section p { font-size: .9rem; } .project-meta { gap: 7px; margin-top: 22px; } .project-meta span { padding: 8px 10px; font-size: .62rem; } .demo-section { padding: 0 16px 80px; } .demo-video-frame { border-radius: 16px; } .intro-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 60px; padding: 20px 20px 90px; } .architecture-section, .features-section, .decision-section, .project-ending { padding: 90px 20px; } .section-heading h2 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 14vw, 5rem); } .architecture-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 12px; } .architecture-arrow { text-align: center; transform: rotate(90deg); } .architecture-node { min-height: 145px; } .architecture-node small { max-width: none; } .architecture-detail { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 34px; margin-top: 70px; padding-top: 60px; } .feature-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .feature-card { min-height: 285px; padding: 23px; } .decision-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 30px; } .project-ending { min-height: 70dvh; } .project-ending h2 { font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 17vw, 5.5rem); }
  }
</style>
